`candidateDetails` is computed eagerly via `Array.from(candidates).map(...).join('\n')` regardless of whether `pass` is `true` or `false`. Since `message` is itself a lazy function, the details string should be computed inside it so it's only evaluated on the failure path:

```ts
return {
  pass,
  message: () => {
    const candidateDetails = Array.from(candidates)
      .map(el => { ... })
      .join('\n');
    return pass
      ? `Expected container NOT to have...`
      : `Expected container to have...\n${candidateDetails || '  (none)'}`;
  },
};
```
